                <pb facs="0062" n="50" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg50"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860F.00/690a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Carr</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-03-17T18:00:00-05:00">March 17, 1939—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. At the press conference today I issued the following statement of the
                    position of this Government toward recent developments in Czechoslovakia:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of press release printed <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >supra</hi>.]</p>
                <p>We hope that you may be able to make this available to the Czechoslovak press and
                    that the latter may find a way to give it publicity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
